From d4775b57e99531a1cf1136e4770538c2df677670 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philip Mueller <claude@philipmueller.ch>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:35:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(harbor_agent): per-sandbox reverse tunnel from the
 sandbox to the model server

For clusters where sandboxes cannot open connections to the training nodes but
the node reaches the sandbox through the provider's service endpoint (OpenSandbox
server proxy, WebSocket). harbor_environment_kwargs.model_tunnel makes
NemoGymSandboxEnvironment upload chisel into every sandbox, run
'chisel server --reverse' there and 'chisel client' on the node, so the sandbox
reaches the model server at 127.0.0.1:<pod_port>. Optional health check GETs
/health through the tunnel before the trial starts. harbor_agent fills
model_tunnel.target with the model server host:port per run. The per-sandbox
chisel credential goes through AUTH, not argv; the provider headers still go
through --header (chisel has no other way).

Signed-off-by: Philip Mueller <claude@philipmueller.ch>
